#
# FR-042 and AC-040. A-032 excludes three things from the committed fixture: a nested .git, the
# Docusaurus website/ scaffold, and a pre-recorded docs/.webster.json. The find walks the
# filesystem rather than the index because two of the three can appear untracked — a .git left
# behind by a test that built in place, a manifest written by a drift.py record that ran against
# the source tree instead of a copy — and either would make one run's results depend on the last
# run's mess.
#
# The last block is the sweep's check on conftest's TOUCH_MAIN_MARKER comment, which says the
# marker line "pushes the cited line src/app/main.py:15 off the @app.post(...) decorator that
# docs/items/create-item.md anchors to". In the committed post-touch tree line 15 is blank and
# the decorator sits on 16; strip the marker and the decorator is back on 15, which is what the
# anchor cites. That comment used to write the page as create-item.md:12 — a line number into a
# file this change may edit, which the docstring above it forbids. The page still carries the
# anchor on line 12, printed here; the citation is gone.

